t-since-libfund-ts t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-libfund_ts\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> ValueType<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> ValueType<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> any_cast<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> any<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> operand<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-libfund-ts t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-libfund_ts\" id=\"Version_5\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> ValueType<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; ValueType<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> any_cast<span class=\"br0\">(</span>any<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> operand<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (5) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-libfund-ts t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Performs type-safe access to the contained object.\n</p><p>For <span class=\"t-v\">(1-3)</span>, the program is ill-formed if <code>ValueType</code> is not a reference and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_copy_constructible\"><span class=\"kw539\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_copy_constructible</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>ValueType<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> operand\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> target <code>any</code> object\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>any_cast<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/add_cv\"><span class=\"kw609\">std::<span class=\"me2\">add_const_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>ValueType<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>operand<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2,3)</span> Returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>any_cast<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>ValueType<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>operand<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4,5)</span> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operand</span></code> is not a null pointer, and the <code>typeid</code> of the requested <code>ValueType</code> matches that of the contents of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operand</span></code>, a pointer to the value contained by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operand</span></code>, otherwise a null pointer.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> Throws <code>bad_any_cast</code> if the <code>typeid</code> of the requested <code>ValueType</code> does not match that of the contents of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operand</span></code>.</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/any","title":"std::experimental::any"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::any_cast","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"5 declarations. Performs type-safe access to the contained object."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"operand"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Returns *any_cast<std::add_const_t<std::remove_reference_t<ValueType>>>(&operand)."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws bad_any_cast if the typeid of the requested ValueType does not match that of the contents of operand."}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":141,"codeBlockCount":0}
